node_modules/
.wrangler/
# Agent session state, including git worktrees checked out under .claude/worktrees. Those hold
# other branches, so without this a `git add -A` would try to commit a second branch into this one.
.claude/
dist/
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example
.env*
# The deploy target (host, user, ports) lives in deploy/hklab/.env.deploy, which `.env*` above
# already ignores. This negation keeps the placeholder template committable, as .dev.vars.example is.
!.env.deploy.example
# Local credentials; never commit.
plans/access.md
*.log
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.venv/
.venv-workers/
python_modules/
.pytest_cache/
# Go build output; `make build` in apps/collector-go writes binaries here.
apps/collector-go/bin/
# A bare `go build` (no -o) drops the binary beside the package; the Makefile writes to bin/.
apps/collector-go/collector
# go.sum is ignored by this machine's global gitignore (~/.gitignore_global), which would strip
# checksums from every Go module here. Repo patterns outrank core.excludesFile, so this negation
# keeps the module verifiable in a fresh clone. Without it the server-side build in golang:1.26-alpine
# resolves dependencies unchecked, or fails outright.
!apps/collector-go/go.sum
